                  %div
                    %p
                      %a{:href => "/nlab/edit/higher+algebra+-+contents"} Edit this sidebar
          %h1#contents Contents
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#idea"} Idea
              %li
                %a{:href => "#statement"} Statement
              %ul
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#in_terms_of_abelian_combinatorial_spectra"} In terms of abelian combinatorial spectra
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#InTermsOfEMModuleSpectra"} In terms of EM-module spectra
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#monoidal_version_in_terms_of_emmodule_specta"} Monoidal version in terms of EM-module specta
              %li
                %a{:href => "#related_concepts"} Related concepts
              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dold-Kan+correspondence"} Dold-Kan correspondence
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stabilization"} stabilizes
            to identify
            %em unbounded
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complexes"} chain complexes
            with certain
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectra"} spectra
          %h2#statement Statement
          %h3#in_terms_of_abelian_combinatorial_spectra In terms of abelian combinatorial spectra
          %p
            The following theorem was established in (
            %a{:href => "#Kan63"}> Kan 63, prop. 5.8
            )
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+unbounded+chain+complexes"} category of unbounded chain complexes
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalent
              to the category of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorial+spectra"} combinatorial spectra
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internalization"} internal
              to
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+groups"} abelian groups
          %p
            Similarly to the unstable case, the above categories, when interpreted as ∞-categories, are also equivalent to the ∞-category of module spectra over the Eilenberg-MacLane ring spectrum of the integers. See the section
            %em
              %a{:href => "module+spectrum#StableDoldKanCorrespondence"} stable Dold-Kan correspondence
            at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module+spectrum"} module spectrum
          %h3#InTermsOfEMModuleSpectra In terms of EM-module spectra
          %p
          #StableDoldKan.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              any
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
              (or
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ringoid"} ringoid
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalence
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                    %mi R
                    %mi ModSpectra
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi Ch
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi R
                    %mi Mod
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    H R ModSpectra
                    \\;\simeq\;
                    Ch_\bullet(R Mod)
            %p
              between a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
              of
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi H
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H R
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module+spectra"} module spectra
              over the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg-MacLane+spectrum"} Eilenberg-MacLane spectrum
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H R
              and the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+unbounded+chain+complexes"} model structure on unbounded chain complexes
              of ordinary
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modules"} modules
            %p
              This presents a corresponding
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} equivalence of (∞,1)-categories
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              is a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+ring"} commutative ring
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} symmetric monoidal (∞,1)-categories
          %p#DerivedCategory
            (Notice that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category+of+a+model+category"} homotopy category
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+unbounded+chain+complexes"}
              model structure on
              = succeed "-chain" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            is the “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+category"}> derived category
            ” of
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mod"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                      %mi Mod
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R Mod
          %p
            This equivalence on the level of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+categories"} homotopy categories
            is due to
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Robinson87"} Robinson 1987
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalence
            is due to
            %a{:href => "#Shipley02"} Shipley 2007, Thm. 1.1
            and
            %a{:href => "#SchwedeShipley03"} Schwede &amp; Shipley 2003, theorem 5.1.6
            (see also the discussion at
            = succeed ")." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+model+categories"} stable model categories
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} equivalence of (∞,1)-categories
            appears as
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Algebra"} Lurie HA, Thm. 7.1.2.13
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mo =
                  %mi ℚ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R = \mathbb{Q}
            the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+numbers"} rational numbers
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StableDoldKan"}
            may be thought of as a stable analog of classical
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+homotopy+theory"} rational homotopy theory
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+stable+homotopy+theory"} rational stable homotopy theory
            for more on this.
          %p More generally:
          #HRAlgerasAreRdgAlgebras.num_theorem
            %h6#theorem_2 Theorem
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+ring"} commutative ring
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zig-zag"} zig-zag
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalences"} Quillen equivalences
              between a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+for+ring+spectra"} model structure for ring spectra
              over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H R
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+dg-algebras"} model structure on dg-algebras
              over
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %p
              In particular the induced
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/total+derived+functors"} total derived functors
              constitute an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence
              of
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+categories"} homotopy categories
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                    %mi R
                    %mi AlgSpec
                    %munderover
                      %mo ≃
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi Θ
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟵
                        %mi H
                    %msub
                      %mi dgAlg
                      %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    H R AlgSpec
                    \\underoverset
                    {\underset{\Theta}{\longrightarrow}}
                    {\overset{H}{\longleftarrow}}
                    {\simeq}
                    dgAlg_R
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Shipley02"}> Shipley 02, theorem 1.1
            )
          #HAModueSpectraAreAdgModules.num_theorem
            %h6#theorem_3 Theorem
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              any
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-algebra"} dg-algebra
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalence
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi H
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi ModSpec
                    %msub
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi Quillen
                    %mi A
                    %mi Mod
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (H A) ModSpec \simeq_{Quillen} A Mod
            %p
              between
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi H
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module+spectra"} module spectra
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-modules"} dg-modules
              over
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %p
              Dually, for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              an
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi H
                      %mi ℤ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H \mathbb{Z}
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+spectrum"} algebra spectrum
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalence
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                    %mi ModSpec
                    %msub
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi Quillen
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Θ
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi Mod
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    E ModSpec \simeq_{Quillen} (\Theta E) Mod
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H(-)
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Θ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Theta(-)
              are from theorem
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HRAlgerasAreRdgAlgebras"}
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#SchwedeShipley03"}> Schwede-Shipley 03, theorem 5.1.6
            ,
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Shipley02"} Shipley 02, corollary 2.15
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} forgetful
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} (∞,1)-functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                    %mi R
                    %mi Mod
                    %mo ⟶
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H R Mod \longrightarrow
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Spectra"} Spectra
              preserves
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-limits"} (∞,1)-limits
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+localization"} simplicial localization
              = succeed ")" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi L
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} (∞,1)-functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi DK
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mi qi
                    %msub
                      %mi Ch
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mo ≃
                    %mi H
                    %mi R
                    %mi Mod
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                    %mi Spectra
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    DK
                    \\;\colon\;
                    L_{qi} Ch_\bullet(R)
                    \\stackrel{\simeq}{\longrightarrow}
                    H R Mod
                    \\stackrel{}{\longrightarrow}
                    Spectra
            %p
              from the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+chain+complexes"} (∞,1)-category of chain complexes
              to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+spectra"} (∞,1)-category of spectra
              which preseres
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-limits"} (∞,1)-limits
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf"} presheaf
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complexes"} chain complexes
              (as it appears in
              = succeed "/" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+sheaf+cohomology"} abelian sheaf cohomology
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hypercohomology"} hypercohomology
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/descent"} descent
              (for some given
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-site"} (∞,1)-site
              structure, hence which is an
              = succeed "/" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-sheaf"} (∞,1)-sheaf
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-stack"} ∞-stack
              of chain complexes) maps under the stable Dold-Kan correspondence
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi DK
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} DK
              to an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-sheaf+of+spectra"} (∞,1)-sheaf of spectra
          .num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              a ring, let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_\bullet(X, R)
              be the standard
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complex"} chain complex
              for
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singular+homology"} singular homology
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_\bullet(X, R)
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              with coefficients in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %p
              Under the stable Dold-Kan correspondence, prop.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StableDoldKan"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smash+product"} smash product
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Σ
                      %mo +
                      %mn ∞
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∧
                    %mi H
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\Sigma^\infty_+ X) \wedge H R
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/suspension+spectrum"} suspension spectrum
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              with the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg-MacLane+spectrum"} Eilenberg-MacLane spectrum
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+homology"} generalized homology
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+groups"} homotopy groups
              of the latter are again singular homology
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Σ
                      %mo +
                      %mn ∞
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∧
                    %mi H
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\pi_\bullet( (\Sigma^\infty_+ X) \wedge H R) \simeq H_\bullet(X, R)
                    \\,.
            %p
              While the correspondence
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Σ
                      %mo +
                      %mn ∞
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∧
                    %mi H
                    %mi R
                    %mo ∼
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\Sigma^\infty_+ X) \wedge H R \sim C_\bullet(X,R)
              under the above equivalence is suggestive, maybe nobody has really checked it in detail. It is sort of stated as true for instance on
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/PS_cache/arxiv/pdf/0906/0906.5198v1.pdf#page=15"} p. 15
              of (
              %a{:href => "#BCT"}> BCT
              ).
          %h3#monoidal_version_in_terms_of_emmodule_specta Monoidal version in terms of EM-module specta
          %p More in detail we have the following statement.
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mo ≔
                  %mi H
                  %mi ℤ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R \coloneqq H \mathbb{Z}
            be the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg-MacLane+spectrum"} Eilenberg-MacLane spectrum
            for the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integers"} integers
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              There is a zig-zag of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+Quillen+adjunction"} lax monoidal
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalences"} Quillen equivalences
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mi Mod
                    %mover
                      %munder
                        %mo ←
                        %mi U
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi Z
                    %msup
                      %mi Sp
                      %mi Σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi sAb
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi ϕ
                            %mo *
                          %mi N
                      %mover
                        %mo ←
                        %mi L
                    %msup
                      %mi Sp
                      %mi Σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Ch
                      %mo +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %munder
                        %mo ←
                        %mi R
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi D
                    %msub
                      %mi Ch
                      %mo •
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    H \mathbb{Z} Mod
                    \\stackrel{\overset{Z}{\longrightarrow}}{\underset{U}{\leftarrow}}
                    Sp^\Sigma(sAb)
                    \\stackrel{\overset{L}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{\phi^* N}{\longrightarrow}}
                    Sp^\Sigma(Ch_+)
                    \\stackrel{\overset{D}{\longrightarrow}}{\underset{R}{\leftarrow}}
                    Ch_\bullet
                    \\,,
            %p
              between
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+model+categories"} monoidal model categories
              satisfying the
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid+axiom+in+a+monoidal+model+category"} monoid axiom in a monoidal model category
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  the model structure for
                  = succeed "-" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi H
                          %mi ℤ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H \mathbb{Z}
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module+spectra"} module spectra
              %li
                %p
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+symmetric+spectrum+objects"} model structure on symmetric spectrum objects
                  in
                  = succeed "s" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+abelian+group"} simplicial abelian group
                  = succeed "es;" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complex"} chain complex
              %li
                %p
                  and the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+chain+complexes"} model structure on chain complexes
                  (unbounded).
            %p
              This induces a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalence
              between the corresponding
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structures+on+monoids"} model structures on monoids
              in these
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal categories
              = succeed "-algebra" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi H
                      %mi ℤ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H \mathbb{Z}
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+dg-algebras"} model structure on dg-algebras
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mi Alg
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi dgAlg
                      %mi ℤ
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    H \mathbb{Z} Alg \simeq dgAlg_\mathbb{Z}
                    \\,.
          %p
            This is due to (
            %a{:href => "#Shipley02"}> Shipley 02
            ). The corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} equivalence of (∞,1)-categories
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            a commutative rings with the intrinsically defined
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/En-algebra"} E1-algebra
            objects on the left appears as (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Algebra"}> Lurie HA, prop. 7.1.4.6
            ). The equivalence on the level of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+categories"} homotopy categories
            was proved in (
            %a{:href => "#Stanley97"}> Stanley 97, theorem 1.1.4
            ).
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              This is a stable version of the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+Dold-Kan+correspondence"} monoidal Dold-Kan correspondence
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-Dold-Kan+correspondence"} ∞-Dold-Kan correspondence
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+stable+homotopy+theory"} rational stable homotopy theory
          %h2#references References
          %ul
            %li#Kan63
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Kan"}> Daniel Kan
                ,
                = succeed "," do
